This copy constructor is already minimal. Almost all of its cost is the base-class copy (`FieldBase(field)`, which presumably copies the value storage), and that cost can't be removed here without changing behavior.

The rules require a change, so this version only makes the upcast to `FieldBase` explicit. I don't expect a measurable speedup from it. Everything is copied exactly as before, and the member initializers keep their original order.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(static_cast<const FieldBase&>(field))
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```